(1978236, 270187, 39629, '<td valign="top">Thanks for those that voted on my entry, and gave such great comments.<br/>To all those that I didnt get to tell,  No I didnt shave her for the challenge, just coincidence that its summer here, and she gets both too hot and too full of matts if she isnt shaved ... She is a much loved pet here and pretty much runs the household, or thinks she does.....She doesnt normally look so peeed off tho, I guess after a day of me following her around with a camera, she was getting annoyed, its her fault tho for being so damn fast and rarely ever sitting still for long</td>', 'Thanks for those that voted on my entry, and gave such great comments.To all those that I didnt get to tell,  No I didnt shave her for the challenge, just coincidence that its summer here, and she gets both too hot and too full of matts if she isnt shaved ... She is a much loved pet here and pretty much runs the household, or thinks she does.....She doesnt normally look so peeed off tho, I guess after a day of me following her around with a camera, she was getting annoyed, its her fault tho for being so damn fast and rarely ever sitting still for long', '2005-12-26 04:33:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(1978315, 269775, 40126, '<td valign="top">i knew it was a blue! congratulations!</td>', 'i knew it was a blue! congratulations!', '2005-12-26 05:47:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1978340, 269314, 24503, '<td valign="top">I like it. I gave it a 7 during the Challenge. The idea is great.<br/>Maybe the composition is a little bit static: all the bottles are at the same distance, so they are the same height. If they were forming a diagonal rather than a pararel line it would improved the photo IMO. And in this way you should also could use a shallow DOF to just focus on one bottle.</td>', 'I like it. I gave it a 7 during the Challenge. The idea is great.Maybe the composition is a little bit static: all the bottles are at the same distance, so they are the same height. If they were forming a diagonal rather than a pararel line it would improved the photo IMO. And in this way you should also could use a shallow DOF to just focus on one bottle.', '2005-12-26 06:46:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1978373, 269775, 28299, '<td valign="top">Well deserved; congrats!</td>', 'Well deserved; congrats!', '2005-12-26 07:27:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1978375, 269314, 3032, '<td valign="top">I think it needs more light from the front because the tone of the bottles is now the same as the background. The bottles should stand out a bit more, especially the part with the text.<br/>I don''t like it how the background works with your foreground subject, the reflection/refraction of the the lights in the bottle is too busy.</td>', 'I think it needs more light from the front because the tone of the bottles is now the same as the background. The bottles should stand out a bit more, especially the part with the text.I don''t like it how the background works with your foreground subject, the reflection/refraction of the the lights in the bottle is too busy.', '2005-12-26 07:31:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(1978390, 269314, 5354, '<td valign="top">I think there''s also a little barrel distortion here. Because of the low angle you have shot from the two outside bottles lean in/bend slightly, this can be fixed in PS.<br/> <br/>As previously noted the background is the same intensity as the foreground, maybe lose some of the light, or increase the light on the foreground subjects.<br/> <br/>There is no single part of the image which the eye wants to rest on, no real main object, maybe try an make a composition where the eye follows a line to end up on a bottle.</td>', 'I think there''s also a little barrel distortion here. Because of the low angle you have shot from the two outside bottles lean in/bend slightly, this can be fixed in PS. As previously noted the background is the same intensity as the foreground, maybe lose some of the light, or increase the light on the foreground subjects. There is no single part of the image which the eye wants to rest on, no real main object, maybe try an make a composition where the eye follows a line to end up on a bottle.', '2005-12-26 07:39:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(1978409, 269061, 28710, '<td valign="top">This is incredible. Looks like a really high end Poser model or something. Wow.<br/> <br/>I''ld love a how-to on getting pictures to look this smooth. It''s not appropriate for every shot, but this is really eye-catching.</td>', 'This is incredible. Looks like a really high end Poser model or something. Wow. I''ld love a how-to on getting pictures to look this smooth. It''s not appropriate for every shot, but this is really eye-catching.', '2005-12-26 08:04:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(1978414, 270187, 28710, '<td valign="top">Sidesplitting. Good one. I love how cat''s just seem to know that we are taking pictures of them. It''s the only time they don''t like being the center of attention.<br/> <br/>The stray tufts add to the picture.</td>', 'Sidesplitting. Good one. I love how cat''s just seem to know that we are taking pictures of them. It''s the only time they don''t like being the center of attention. The stray tufts add to the picture.', '2005-12-26 08:09:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(1978419, 270507, 28710, '<td valign="top">Interesting choice of background. The blues really complement each other well.<br/> <br/>I wonder if it''s just me being weird, but I noticed that there were 3 A''s in your title (having used An AmpersAnd instead of an ''and'') and 3 A''s in your battery.<br/> <br/>I wonder if these things were intentional.<br/> <br/>Regardless, very nicely done. The only thing I really didn''t care for was that the lid has been very obviously removed and placed in such a way to indicate that this is a totally manufactured pic. Doesn''t take anything away from the pic though.</td>', 'Interesting choice of background. The blues really complement each other well. I wonder if it''s just me being weird, but I noticed that there were 3 A''s in your title (having used An AmpersAnd instead of an ''and'') and 3 A''s in your battery. I wonder if these things were intentional. Regardless, very nicely done. The only thing I really didn''t care for was that the lid has been very obviously removed and placed in such a way to indicate that this is a totally manufactured pic. Doesn''t take anything away from the pic though.', '2005-12-26 08:17:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(1978423, 269775, 43774, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Owen!!!!!</td>', 'Congratulations Owen!!!!!', '2005-12-26 08:17:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1978431, 270212, 28710, '<td valign="top">Very nice pic. I LOVE the way you used lens flare (I have recently learned the proper term is "aperture ghosting").<br/> <br/>It really gave it a PJ from space look.<br/> <br/>Great execution.</td>', 'Very nice pic. I LOVE the way you used lens flare (I have recently learned the proper term is "aperture ghosting"). It really gave it a PJ from space look. Great execution.', '2005-12-26 08:21:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(1978440, 269251, 29490, '<td valign="top">Good pun.  It just didn''t grab my eye for some reason.  Does appear oversharpened.  I think I would have liked to see more of a "nature scene" made with the chocolate, like a pond and lilies and bullwinkle was walking through that; or maybe somebody sitting at a table with fork, ready to eat mr moose - albeit with a quizzical look on their face.  Hmmmm.  Or maybe a persimmon?<br/> <br/>Merry Christmas. :)<br/> <br/>Edit<br/>I think when looking at the photo I''m trying to decide if the moose is chocolate or is it wood; I think this mental debate, especially for someone of my limited mental facilities, obviously took away from my photo-enjoyment.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-12-26 08:37:40.</i></td>', 'Good pun.  It just didn''t grab my eye for some reason.  Does appear oversharpened.  I think I would have liked to see more of a "nature scene" made with the chocolate, like a pond and lilies and bullwinkle was walking through that; or maybe somebody sitting at a table with fork, ready to eat mr moose - albeit with a quizzical look on their face.  Hmmmm.  Or maybe a persimmon? Merry Christmas. :) EditI think when looking at the photo I''m trying to decide if the moose is chocolate or is it wood; I think this mental debate, especially for someone of my limited mental facilities, obviously took away from my photo-enjoyment.', '2005-12-26 08:23:23.000000', '2005-12-26 08:37:40.000000', 0),
