(1979066, 269251, 16106, '<td valign="top">I think you hurt yourself with the lighting here. This sort of bright uniform white works well with fur or leather product shots, where the surface is very complex and will carry the image, but the simplicity of the moose needs more dramatic lighting, with a more varied backround. The image is just too static and simple. Had the moose been standing in a pool of mouse rather than bars of chocolate, and the lighing implied a sunset/nature setup, the pun might have run a bit further.</td>', 'I think you hurt yourself with the lighting here. This sort of bright uniform white works well with fur or leather product shots, where the surface is very complex and will carry the image, but the simplicity of the moose needs more dramatic lighting, with a more varied backround. The image is just too static and simple. Had the moose been standing in a pool of mouse rather than bars of chocolate, and the lighing implied a sunset/nature setup, the pun might have run a bit further.', '2005-12-26 14:56:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(1979078, 269314, 16106, '<td valign="top">I think you cropped a bit too close to the bottom of the frame, and that the botles bleed into the backround because of two factors, the lighting is too universal, a flash or spot picking them ou would have popped them forward; and the focus is too soft if the bottles were crisper they would have seperated more strongly from the BG which is nicely fuzzy.<br/> <br/>The strand of lights woven through the bottle isn''t cutting it, too subtle, either bigger lights or brighter lights (longer exposure and don''t light the tree for part of  the time?) could help, otherwise just loose the strand.</td>', 'I think you cropped a bit too close to the bottom of the frame, and that the botles bleed into the backround because of two factors, the lighting is too universal, a flash or spot picking them ou would have popped them forward; and the focus is too soft if the bottles were crisper they would have seperated more strongly from the BG which is nicely fuzzy. The strand of lights woven through the bottle isn''t cutting it, too subtle, either bigger lights or brighter lights (longer exposure and don''t light the tree for part of  the time?) could help, otherwise just loose the strand.', '2005-12-26 15:06:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(1979097, 269480, 50034, '<td valign="top"><b>"Je'' taime le cafe''!"</b>  Pardon my French, but I hope I got it right!<br/>Perfecto!  Magnifique!  Right on target!  (Just covering all the bases linguistically!)<br/>Color is on the money &amp; really sells the subject!<br/>     Your pun is soooooo...me!!!  Thank you, Thank you, Thank you, Thank you..........(ad infinitum/ad nauseum)<br/>Cafe (brown) Coffee...Pour ol'' nose...Elephant of a pun...<br/><b>"Drink coffee while driving for thirty miles to the bladder!" ;)</b></td>', '"Je'' taime le cafe''!"  Pardon my French, but I hope I got it right!Perfecto!  Magnifique!  Right on target!  (Just covering all the bases linguistically!)Color is on the money & really sells the subject!     Your pun is soooooo...me!!!  Thank you, Thank you, Thank you, Thank you..........(ad infinitum/ad nauseum)Cafe (brown) Coffee...Pour ol'' nose...Elephant of a pun..."Drink coffee while driving for thirty miles to the bladder!" ;)', '2005-12-26 15:19:37.000000', NULL, 0),
