(1979130, 269775, 4285, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the votes, favorites and great comments.<br/> <br/>A couple of people wondered how it was done.  Basically all I did was rig an eye dropper with a syringe to control the drop.  I then set it up in front of a picture of an eye on my monitor and positioned it the way it looked best and shot it (I used one of my clamp lights turned upside down as a holder).</td>', 'Thanks for the votes, favorites and great comments. A couple of people wondered how it was done.  Basically all I did was rig an eye dropper with a syringe to control the drop.  I then set it up in front of a picture of an eye on my monitor and positioned it the way it looked best and shot it (I used one of my clamp lights turned upside down as a holder).', '2005-12-26 15:54:18.000000', NULL, 0),
