(1979921, 269961, 37893, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Brenb:</b></div><hr/><i> Just had to say I can''t believe anyone actually thought I would put a fish eye inside a lens. :)  I just printed a photo of one and cut it out and put it on the front of the len.  I enjoyed the comments and thanks for the nice votes too.<br/>And this was the best comment of all: Hehehheeh! Funny. Almost a "scalvert" image here. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi Bren! Woot! That was me!!!! This image was pretty sweet though I think it would have been more convincing had the image been adhered to the "inside" of the filter and not the front. Now that I see the edges of the paper ;) Anyway, 21st place is a good place to be in ;) I wish I could say that for my image :(<br/> <br/>Great job!<br/> <br/>Rikki</td>', 'Originally posted by Brenb: Just had to say I can''t believe anyone actually thought I would put a fish eye inside a lens. :)  I just printed a photo of one and cut it out and put it on the front of the len.  I enjoyed the comments and thanks for the nice votes too.And this was the best comment of all: Hehehheeh! Funny. Almost a "scalvert" image here.   Hi Bren! Woot! That was me!!!! This image was pretty sweet though I think it would have been more convincing had the image been adhered to the "inside" of the filter and not the front. Now that I see the edges of the paper ;) Anyway, 21st place is a good place to be in ;) I wish I could say that for my image :( Great job! Rikki', '2005-12-26 22:40:07.000000', NULL, 0),
